        Item("S199", "Q", "Symbol-confusion warning.", "ON: ticker/name duplicates obscure which exact mint social traffic references; OFF: contract-mint references are unambiguous.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S200", "Q", "Multi-platform organic spread.", "ON: independently authored mentions grow across two distinct communities and on-chain buyers subsequently increase; OFF: cross-posting originates from one campaign.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S201", "Q", "Narrative half-life.", "ON: new mentions decay faster than holder/flow growth, suggesting brief fad; OFF: genuine repeat interest persists.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S202", "Q", "Meme remix momentum.", "ON: independently created derivatives/edits increase while original token retains net buying; OFF: cloned campaigns inflate counts without genuine interest.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S203", "Q", "Event catalyst authenticity.", "ON: a verifiable external event precedes flow shift in exact mint; OFF: claimed catalyst is fabricated, old or not connected to token.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S204", "Q", "Social-onchain decoupling.", "ON: social excitement grows while distinct buyers, quote inflow and executable mark fall; OFF: flow independently catches up.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S205", "R", "Wash-loop suspicion.", "ON: same linked wallets repeatedly alternate buys and sells with little net exposure change; OFF: independent funding and lasting positions contradict common control.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S206", "R", "Funding-cluster dominance.", "ON: nominally distinct buyers share recent common funding and dominate volume; OFF: economic independence can be established.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S207", "R", "Creator/insider dump.", "ON: proven creator-linked wallets remove substantial tradable supply into outside purchases; OFF: association or sale interpretation is disproved.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S208", "R", "Mint authority hazard.", "ON: unexpected live mint authority can expand supply beyond strategy's accepted token design; OFF: on-chain authority is revoked or risk is intentionally modelled.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S209", "R", "Freeze/transfer restriction hazard.", "ON: permissions/extensions may prevent selling or freeze balances, confirmed by program state or simulation; OFF: verified normal transfers and sell simulation resolve issue.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S210", "R", "Malicious transfer-fee exposure.", "ON: Token-2022 or custom token transfer fees materially exceed price model / policy; OFF: verified actual transfer fee is acceptable and priced.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S211", "R", "Liquidity drain.", "ON: sudden real sell-depth collapse accompanies vault removal or abnormal pool operation; OFF: verified migration points to healthy successor liquidity.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S212", "R", "Phantom peak.", "ON: a tick implies implausible price multiple absent from reserves, executed proceeds and neighboring actual trades; OFF: independent pool math and meaningful fills verify the level.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S213", "R", "Spoofed volume.", "ON: reported volume lacks corresponding on-chain swap notional or repeatedly double-counts split routes; OFF: all signatures and balance deltas reconcile.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S214", "R", "Honeypot / unsellable route.", "ON: a normal-size test sell fails on a verified active venue despite apparent buys; OFF: fresh executable test sell and real fills succeed.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S215", "R", "Pool impersonation.", "ON: token name/symbol matches but mint/program/pool identity does not; OFF: cryptographic mint and verified venue match intended asset.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S216", "R", "Post-dump prolonged decay.", "ON: token is old relative to its lane, price below valid anchored VWAP, new buyers shrinking and no reversal structure; OFF: credible new demand and structure appear.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S217", "S", "Structure trailing exit.", "ON: closes breach latest confirmed higher low with real sell pressure; OFF: structure remains intact, so continue managing thesis.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S218", "S", "Momentum rollover.", "ON: price acceleration turns negative for successive windows as positive flow decays; OFF: speed and breadth recover above local base.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S219", "S", "Volume climax distribution.", "ON: extreme genuine turnover prints a wide upper wick and net sellers dominate after it; OFF: new highs are accepted with restored demand.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S220", "S", "Flow-led scale-out.", "ON: price holds a high while early profitable holders distribute and independent new buyers no longer offset them; OFF: new-money inflow covers sales.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S221", "S", "Exit-value drawdown.", "ON: size-adjusted executable net sell proceeds fall from prior *trusted executable* peak by tested amount; OFF: only untrusted chart prints show drawdown.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S222", "S", "Thesis time stop.", "ON: expected breakout/recovery has not occurred within matched setup lifespan and after-cost edge decays; OFF: a fresh qualifying setup explicitly replaces old thesis.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S223", "S", "Protect capital after expansion.", "ON: position has achieved an after-cost profit milestone and structural conditions justify partial de-risking; OFF: test shows premature scaling harms expected payoff.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S224", "S", "Runner hold authorization.", "ON: genuine higher lows, positive net flow, new buyers and viable exit quotes persist; OFF: two independent evidence families fail together.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S225", "S", "Liquidity-first emergency exit.", "ON: significant executable sell-depth deterioration threatens ability to liquidate; OFF: healthy sell path and normalized depth return.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S226", "S", "Exit route escape.", "ON: primary sell execution fails or expires while alternate independently verified route is usable; OFF: no valid path exists, triggering incident management.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S227", "S", "Stop re-entry whipsaw.", "ON: recently stopped token retakes former level with fresh independent flow and a genuinely new setup; OFF: only price bounce without new evidence.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S228", "S", "After-cost profit-lock logic.", "ON: current size-adjusted confirmed liquidation proceeds exceed entry basis and available downside exceeds selected risk budget; OFF: reported P&L relies on displayed midpoint rather than executable proceeds.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S229", "T", "Verified program/venue identity.", "ON: exact mint, active program, state and pool mapping match authoritative accounts; OFF: suffix, symbol or vendor label is the only evidence.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S230", "T", "Reserve-price cross-check.", "ON: computed marginal and size-specific AMM/curve prices reconcile with fetched reserve state and fees; OFF: mismatch exceeds model and timestamp tolerance.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S231", "T", "Freshness within horizon.", "ON: receive-time delay plus processing time fits strategy's time-to-live; OFF: opportunity has expired even if historical setup remains profitable.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S232", "T", "Event-order completion.", "ON: historical seed, live stream and gap replay reconcile by slot/signature without reordering causal features; OFF: late old events contaminate current decision.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S233", "T", "Missing-vs-negative discriminator.", "ON: absent candles/wallet history are tagged unknown with completeness score, not zero flow or price collapse; OFF: valid negative observations replace unknown state.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S234", "T", "Two independent price measurements.", "ON: reliable reserve-derived mark and actual executable sell quote directionally agree at same slot/size; OFF: one source is stale or wrong venue.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S235", "T", "Buy quote confirmation.", "ON: buy quote reflects actual input size, destination mint, fees and current state within allowed deviation; OFF: transaction would be materially worse than thesis.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S236", "T", "Sell-path readiness.", "ON: position's exact token quantity can be simulated/quoted for a sell via actual available venue; OFF: simulation or route is absent.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S237", "T", "Entry-basis immutability.", "ON: position basis equals independently reconciled confirmed fills plus costs and remains immutable; OFF: paper mark or later snapshot overwrites real fill.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S238", "T", "Canonical position reconciliation.", "ON: wallet balance, sellable quantity, position ledger, signatures and pending transactions converge; OFF: orphan transfer or unknown holding remains unresolved.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S239", "T", "Prediction provenance.", "ON: a model's feature snapshot, version, timestamp and realized forward label are reproducible without lookahead; OFF: labels use phantom highs or decision-time future events.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("S240", "T", "Protective-exit independence.", "ON: stop/protective sell can execute even when entry model or FDG has a disagreement; OFF: the sell is improperly blocked by an entry-only score/gate.", Kind.EVIDENCE, emptyList()),
        Item("T241", "U", "Organic first-wave ignition", "`[0–45s; launch curve; microcap]` **Trigger:** unrelated first buyers grow across several ten-second slices; genuine net quote inflow rises and reserves validate [S001 S005 S097]. **Fail:** linked wallets create the wave or two subsequent windows turn net-sell. **Manage:** take a size supported by round-trip economics; trail the first confirmed higher low, not an arbitrary early profit percentage.", Kind.ENTRY, listOf("S001", "S005", "S097")),
        Item("T242", "U", "Initial sell absorbed", "`[15–120s; launch curve]` **Trigger:** a meaningful early holder sells, level holds, and at least a second independent buyer cohort takes over [S004 S008 S089]. **Fail:** that sell-defined low breaks on new outflow. **Manage:** watch seller's remaining supply; preserve exposure while new buyers refill the book-equivalent curve demand.", Kind.ENTRY, listOf("S004", "S008", "S089")),
        Item("T243", "U", "Flat start, genuine acceleration", "`[30s–3m; microcap]` **Trigger:** quiet first minute establishes honest support; new wallets start funding buys, volume expands and first micro-range breaks [S007 S079 S081]. **Fail:** breakout re-enters base without independent bids. **Manage:** do not buy a sudden one-wallet candle; allow short retest if the actual price and fresh quote agree.", Kind.ENTRY, listOf("S007", "S079", "S081")),
        Item("T244", "U", "Launch staircase", "`[20s–4m; curve]` **Trigger:** rising 15–30s lows, widening buyer cohort and increasing genuine flow coincide [S009 S085 S098]. **Fail:** latest higher low fails and buy imbalance flips negative. **Manage:** potential runner hold while successive lows stay higher; scale only if executable sell depth supports expansion.", Kind.ENTRY, listOf("S009", "S085", "S098")),
        Item("T245", "U", "False opening crash", "`[30s–5m; curve]` **Trigger:** early dump creates a lower wick, trade price and sell quote recover, and new independent buyers initiate [S062 S099 S170]. **Fail:** second sell attack undercuts flush low. **Manage:** treat as reversal setup with a short time limit; never assume that every dump is a buying opportunity.", Kind.ENTRY, listOf("S062", "S099", "S170")),
        Item("T246", "U", "Launch second-wave handoff", "`[1–8m; microcap]` **Trigger:** first buyers pause or partially exit while new wallet cohort drives a confirmed high and stays net-buying [S003 S088 S161]. **Fail:** only originals trade and later buyers stop entering. **Manage:** evaluate continued trend; do not penalize ordinary first-wave profit-taking if net new money absorbs it.", Kind.ENTRY, listOf("S003", "S088", "S161")),
        Item("T247", "V", "Curve reserve staircase", "`[1–15m; verified bonding curve]` **Trigger:** true quote reserves rise in a steady sequence with broad buys; price remains near legitimate trend [S013 S015 S022]. **Fail:** reserve growth reverses and market flow stays negative. **Manage:** size using curve-specific two-sided quotes and update expected graduation timing dynamically.", Kind.ENTRY, listOf("S013", "S015", "S022")),
        Item("T248", "V", "Curve stall-and-restart", "`[1–20m; curve]` **Trigger:** reserve progression stalls in narrow price range, selling contracts, and independent new-money flow restarts [S019 S023 S077]. **Fail:** genuine sell activity pushes below stall low. **Manage:** first objective is previous curve high; continue only if demand actually carries through.", Kind.ENTRY, listOf("S019", "S023", "S077")),
        Item("T249", "V", "Curve sell-sponge", "`[1–15m; curve]` **Trigger:** a sizeable insider/early bag exit is visible, yet price damage diminishes across sells as newcomers buy [S016 S076 S123]. **Fail:** identified supply overhang continues to exceed new-money absorption. **Manage:** monitor insider balances and execute the sell path at planned size before commitment.", Kind.ENTRY, listOf("S016", "S076", "S123")),
        Item("T250", "V", "Graduating demand broadens", "`[progress near verified threshold, not fixed market cap]` **Trigger:** completion probability rises because actual reserve state approaches threshold while later cohorts expand [S020 S024 S085]. **Fail:** flow dies or verified completion state disagrees with prediction. **Manage:** explicitly transition pricing/route state on migration; do not carry curve quotes into the AMM.", Kind.ENTRY, listOf("S020", "S024", "S085")),
        Item("T251", "V", "Curve pullback-to-progress shelf", "`[2–30m; curve]` **Trigger:** a temporary reserve setback creates a support shelf, repeated tests see smaller sell bursts, then quote inflow returns [S023 S080 S149]. **Fail:** shelf fails with negative net flow. **Manage:** target prior progress zone, then reassess: no automatic graduation bet.", Kind.ENTRY, listOf("S023", "S080", "S149")),
        Item("T252", "V", "Curve trend with efficient size", "`[15s–30m; any cap with viable curve]` **Trigger:** early verified trend remains intact, but large proposed entry loses edge; a smaller size retains positive after-cost margin [S021 S135 S141]. **Fail:** *all* useful sizes have nonpositive executable margin. **Manage:** downsize rather than invent a high fixed market-cap floor or add arbitrary admission gates.", Kind.ENTRY, listOf("S021", "S135", "S141")),
        Item("T253", "W", "Verified migration opening drive", "`[0–90s after migration]` **Trigger:** new pool is cryptographically linked and live; distinct new-pool buyers move price and executable liquidation value higher [S025 S027 S038]. **Fail:** pool/venue identity unresolved, sell simulation fails or opening low breaks. **Manage:** start separate pool-local chart and watch first-minute opening high.", Kind.ENTRY, listOf("S025", "S027", "S038")),
        Item("T254", "W", "Migration dip defended", "`[1–10m after migration]` **Trigger:** real new-pool sells briefly undercut opening value, then fresh buyers reclaim it with working exit route [S029 S032 S036]. **Fail:** recovery cannot hold pool-open price. **Manage:** first partial objective opening high; runner hold only if new-pool breadth expands.", Kind.ENTRY, listOf("S029", "S032", "S036")),
        Item("T255", "W", "First opening-range break", "`[1–15m after migration]` **Trigger:** a verified new-pool range builds; buy volume and new holders expand through its high [S037 S047 S081]. **Fail:** price returns beneath the range with sell-flow dominance. **Manage:** trail new AMM swing lows; ignore historical curve-only phantom highs.", Kind.ENTRY, listOf("S037", "S047", "S081")),
        Item("T256", "W", "Pool VWAP hold and second leg", "`[2–20m after migration]` **Trigger:** opening impulse cools above pool-local VWAP and a fresh independently funded buyer wave breaks out [S039 S048 S033]. **Fail:** VWAP breaks and cohorts reverse. **Manage:** hold continuation, not a perpetual graduation thesis.", Kind.ENTRY, listOf("S033", "S039", "S048")),
        Item("T257", "W", "Liquidity-upgrade entry", "`[after confirmed venue switch]` **Trigger:** fresh AMM makes real sell depth materially better, healthy buy activity continues and round-trip economics improve [S030 S041 S140]. **Fail:** purported depth is stale or pool quote collapses. **Manage:** recalculate trade size from post-migration impact, not pre-migration market cap.", Kind.ENTRY, listOf("S030", "S041", "S140")),
        Item("T258", "W", "Graduation trap avoidance / later reclaim", "`[opening 1–30m]` **Trigger:** initial markup was sold by holders, but a *later* new base forms and independent buys recover opening resistance [S034 S042 S048]. **Fail:** distribution resumes before confirmed reclaim. **Manage:** no trade on the initial spike; only open once the second structure exists.", Kind.ENTRY, listOf("S034", "S042", "S048")),
        Item("T259", "X", "One-minute range release", "`[2–60m; curve or AMM]` **Trigger:** compressed real range breaks above resistance with volume leading and broad buyers [S162 S160 S161]. **Fail:** next window trades back inside range on net sells. **Manage:** first risk anchor is inside-range invalidation; continue only if expansion has actual sell-value gains.", Kind.ENTRY, listOf("S160", "S161", "S162")),
